                    "*Connecting electrolytic capacitors backwards can cause them to explode.  Make sure that the negative terminal of the capacitor (marked with the white stripe) is always at a lower voltage than the positive terminal and that the voltage across the capacitor doesn't exceed the capacitor's voltage rating."
